---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Card } from '@weluvabid/iris/components';
import { withBase } from '@lib/journal';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Journal"
  description="How I approach software engineering and the things I like building."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-muted-foreground">About</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
      I like finding out what happens underneath.
    </h1>

    <div class="prose-journal mt-8">
      <p>
        I'm Abid, a software engineer. My name is technically Abith, thanks to a spelling mistake my
        grandfather made, but I go by Abid. I really enjoy digging into code. Sometimes I’ll just
        look at documentation or go through source code. Sometimes I just like building things from
        scratch so I can learn how everything works.
      </p>
      <p>
        This has led me to work on a wide range of problems. Caching, serialisation, storage
        engines, language tooling, reactive runtimes, browser extensions, frontend architectures.
        Some were driven by a need, but most were driven by the question I couldn’t get out of my
        head. Either way, I enjoy both.
      </p>
      <p>
        I enjoy getting into detail, but I don’t think complex code is always good code. I enjoy
        having a stable implementation that's predictable, testable and easy to follow. I enjoy
        automating repetitive tasks rather than making every developer remember another step. I
        prefer to measure a performance improvement rather than just say something is fast.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also enjoy working on the product side of engineering. Why do we need this? How will users
        use this? How can we avoid any nasty edge cases? While I enjoy the implementation side, I
        also enjoy the actual product.
      </p>
      <p>
        Not every experiment will be a product. Some are just tools or proofs of concept. There’s
        always something to learn when working with real code in a constrained environment.
      </p>
    </div>

    <Card.Root class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-border bg-muted/40">
      <Card.Header>
        <Card.Title>Have a look around</Card.Title>
        <Card.Description>
          The projects show what I've built. The writings show some of the thinking behind them.
        </Card.Description>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-3 pt-3">
          <a class="text-sm font-medium underline underline-offset-4" href={withBase('/projects/')}>
            Projects
          </a>
          <a class="text-sm font-medium underline underline-offset-4" href={withBase('/journal/')}>
            Writings
          </a>
          <a
            class="text-sm font-medium underline underline-offset-4"
            href="https://github.com/weluvabid"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
          >
            GitHub
          </a>
        </div>
      </Card.Header>
    </Card.Root>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
